 "limitations": [
  "Winning is not randomly assigned; frontrunners may differ in unobserved buzz. The placebo and pre-trend tests check for diverging trends but cannot rule out all confounding, so the estimate is reported as an association.",
  "Event-study pre-period coefficients are jointly insignificant but mostly negative, meaning winners were already gaining slightly before the ceremony; part of the post-ceremony gap may be pre-existing momentum.",
  "Many losing nominees had already closed by Tony night, so the control group is smaller and made of surviving productions.",
  "Gross is only observed while a show runs; losers that close drop out, which likely biases the gross effect toward zero. Closure is analyzed separately.",
  "Nominees that closed before Tony night, and titles that could not be matched unambiguously to the weekly grosses, are excluded.",
  "Gross is box-office revenue, not profit."
 ]
